{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/pulls/149","id":4733607032,"node_id":"PR_kwDOTEdTLM8AAAABGiUceA","html_url":"https://github.com/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/pull/149","diff_url":"https://github.com/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/pull/149.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/pull/149.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/issues/149","number":149,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Prove projected OSD for played-legal finite-history policies","user":{"login":"jicheng9617","id":74550583,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc0NTUwNTgz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/74550583?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jicheng9617","html_url":"https://github.com/jicheng9617","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jicheng9617/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jicheng9617/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jicheng9617/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jicheng9617/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jicheng9617/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jicheng9617/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jicheng9617/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jicheng9617/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jicheng9617/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Contribution scope\r\n\r\nAlgorithm 2.2 now has a genuine finite-history support-policy recurrence. Its fixed, decreasing-step and tuned guarantees require support legality only at the actual played points; an off-path oracle law is optional. Both untuned bounds keep the negative terminal distance. Canonical bridges recover the previous chooser exactly.\r\n\r\nStacked on **PR #148**, exact base `b1ffe6322ceef5492c3931a0e40f7e7d5fa5ff21` (`codex/research-online-guessing-osd`), which is OPEN/draft and unmerged. This PR does not claim main or the live site changed.\r\n\r\n- Type/route: theorem-edge and reusable-interface; Online Learning Chapter 2 / `online-osd-policy`.\r\n- Source: Orabona arXiv:1912.13213v10 (21 June 2026), Algorithm 2.2 and Lemma 2.31, printed 19–21 / PDF 31–33; explicit Theorem 2.13 / equation (2.1) transfer, printed 13–15 / PDF 25–27. Frozen PDF SHA256 `cef4edfa97a6e063e53e9c532717c50aa156e5bc782ea49f969b3385011a1b17`.\r\n- Manifest: `research-wiki/contribution-contracts/ONLINE-OSD-POLICY-20261004.json`.\r\n- Public module: `BanditRLProof/OnlineSubgradientPolicy.lean` (21 frozen theorems, 30 total public declarations); actual canaries: `Tests/OnlineSubgradientPolicyCanary.lean` (74 theorems).\r\n\r\n## Reuse and semantic boundary\r\n\r\nActual project/Mathlib declaration retrieval and typed signatures preceded tactics. Reuse the shared `OnlineSubgradientDescent.lemma_2_31`, finite-loss/support APIs, `OnlineGradientDescent.project_spec` and `weighted_potential_sum`; no new per-Book project, projection theory copy or large dependency/toolchain upgrade. New declarations produce a genuine path rather than consume a supplied step-regret bound.\r\n\r\nThe policy is one fixed exogenous deterministic function of finite past whole losses, actual output history and the current whole loss. Prefix equality keeps that policy and initialization fixed. This is pathwise full-information mathematics, without stochastic-law/measurability/independence or executable-oracle claims. Fixed eta is positive, permits T=0 and does not require bounded V. Variable eta requires a positive horizon, positive nonincreasing played rates and bounded pairwise distances; the final denominator is eta(T-1). Tuning uses D,G,T>0 and actual selected-vector norms on that same prescribed horizon run.\r\n\r\nFormalizer `/root`, fresh clean v3 decoder `/root/normal_blind`, distinct source/reader actor `/root/source_reviewer`; requested GPT-6 Astra/medium. Source contract, actual body and repaired final reader are accepted-with-explicit-delta; no independent human or external-model review claim. The v2 contaminated blind packet remains diagnostic, and the original canary and rejected reader versions remain intact. Source attribution was repaired by removing three structural/algorithm source-theorem cards: those results remain explicitly documented as library refinements/adapters; the four actual source-performance cards remain.\r\n\r\n- [x] Exact source anchor, formulas, assumptions/deltas, proof bridges and folded Lean are visible.\r\n- [x] Fresh blind reconstruction and distinct source review; proof-body/canary and full reader gates are separate.\r\n- [x] Frozen statements, definition context and premise lists unchanged; explicit historical Test supersession only.\r\n- [x] Source/structural attribution and remaining chapter boundary visible.\r\n\r\n## Book and graph integration\r\n\r\nAll Books use the same declaration registry. Add one source-qualified Book route with 21 specific theorem notes, four main previews and four source-performance cards. Retain older links and their canonical scope. Lean Graph adds 30 public nodes; overview route updated. No certified cross-setting functor was found: this extends the policy interface for the same Euclidean support/projection mechanism. Actual native proof-value extraction passes 21 required edges (30 scope / 473 boundary / 2,325 scoped edges); teaching links are separate.\r\n\r\nBandit results, Source Chapters 13–17 spine and unrelated roadmap have no mathematical change. The task-local frontier is accepted; the historical global SGB pointer is unchanged. Full chapter/book completion remains false. Versioned `program-milestone.json` records the current terminal status without rewriting frozen candidate inventory bytes. Required follow-ups include Chapter 2 causal linearization, unit/scaling and scalar tuning/source-ledger boundaries, 26 older production-path review/contributor migrations and all remaining Chapters 3–16/main-text appendix dependencies.\r\n\r\n## Verification\r\n\r\n- [x] Required contributor/protocol/skill and paper workflow files audited; exact base contributor gate passes all eight production paths.\r\n- [x] Actual public focused build: 3,320 jobs; actual Test focused build: 3,324 jobs.\r\n- [x] Shared root: 9,083 jobs; Tests: 9,220 jobs; full `python tools/bandit.py check`: 466 tests, seven existing skips.\r\n- [x] 122 named public/Test `#check` and `#print axioms`: only propext/Classical.choice/Quot.sound or none.\r\n- [x] Nondegenerate opposite-history selections, false off-path law with legal play, exact fixed regret/energy/positive residual, nonconstant harmonic steps, invalid future prefix, genuine empty-support fallback with proven nonlegality and actual T=0 bound with positive cancelling endpoints.\r\n- [x] Actual final04 site build/check: 937 pages, 835 modules, 10,721 declarations, 257 highlights. Unchanged search fence: 1,499,464 < 1,500,000 bytes.\r\n- [x] All 30 canonical registry node hashes match actual Lean headers. Repaired final reader: 409 raw bindings; fixed input inventory: 407; immutable audit: 1,272 reviewed raw rows including explicit historical canary preservation.\r\n- [x] `git diff --check` for every changed code/contract/metadata/receipt/script path; exact raw compiler `.log` files are excluded because their original whitespace must stay byte-identical. The whole-delta raw-log whitespace finding is preserved separately. No placeholders, hidden extra axioms, generated `_site` edits or whole-book completion claim.\r\n\r\nEvidence: `runs/online-osd-policy-20261004/accepted-decision.json`, `accepted-binding-audit.json`, `final-reader-receipt-v2.json`, real command logs/exits and scoped compiled dependencies. Initial tracking-only full-harness failure, canary arithmetic repairs and source-attribution reader rejection are retained; they are not acceptance evidence.\r\n\r\n## Provenance and reviewer notes\r\n\r\nIntentional Lean contribution under the repository MIT license; mathematical source credited to Orabona. Shared library/registry expanded in the isolated research worktree without overwriting canonical main or unrelated worktrees. Automated source review artifacts contain no private human review or credentials. Temporary checkout, shared links and unique ignored source/browser/graph artifacts are retained for ongoing book work. No merge/deployment is included.\r\n","created_at":"2026-10-04T10:20:09Z","updated_at":"2026-10-04T10:22:06Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"b1eeedf74cc74c0a6768f88a635a80251c1e2c34","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":true,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/pulls/149/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/pulls/149/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/issues/149/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/statuses/410693c31d8e1343c6b023886304520c2a834a11","head":{"label":"DakeBU:codex/research-online-osd-policy","ref":"codex/research-online-osd-policy","sha":"410693c31d8e1343c6b023886304520c2a834a11","user":{"login":"DakeBU","id":159223240,"node_id":"U_kgDOCX2NyA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/159223240?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DakeBU","html_url":"https://github.com/DakeBU","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DakeBU/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DakeBU/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DakeBU/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/user